title CAUM3 — the whole Mikrophone firmware loop carries only the committed run to the wire
prompt recur the 1024-round itinerary Lindy-first crux-first; take the next agent-doable lap on the road past BUHR, approve own design rounds, send each finished increment as its own signed round, stop at custody gates
think Read REMEMBER (custody gates 1–6), the 1024-round itinerary, and the six-season double-seat expansion. Living edge = Season A's Mikrophone firmware journey (waymark CAUM); CAUM0 (session that forgets), CAUM1 (wire frame from carry), CAUM2 (recorder control state machine) all GREEN.
think Lindy-first, crux-first: three rungs stand proven alone but the composition is unwitnessed. The whole firmware gesture — press record, keep on purpose, set down, carry only the kept capture across the wire — is the most durable next move: it is read for years through the one path that ties the three, and it opens every surface above onto a spine known whole.
think Chose a new module mikrophone/firmware.rye over editing the landed CAUM2 file — one-file-per-rung matches the journey. It composes, inventing nothing: commit delegates to session.commit, power_down to session.power_down, carry_frame to wire.frame over the recorder's session (a public field, reached as &rec.ses), carried_bytes to wire.deframe.
think Self-approved the design round (20260814-022312) before implementing, per the itinerary's filling law. Four invariants: whole loop round-trips byte-for-byte; only the committed crosses even with an uncommitted tail; a forgotten run powered down carries NothingToCarry with an empty working buffer; a tampered frame refuses DigestMismatch before a byte is yielded.
obs The uncommitted-tail case is the sharp one — commit "keep", feed "X" while still recording, stop; the wire carries exactly "keep" because carry_frame reads the committed carry, not the live working buffer. It fuses CAUM2's control, CAUM0's deliberate commit, and CAUM1's framed carry in a single scenario.
obs Custody untouched — no disk, no network, no key signs, no funds; the Sha256 stays an integrity check the far side recomputes, not a signature. Real hardware (record button, microphone, wire) stays custody gate #2; a signed carry stays a later gated rung. No custody gate reached this round.
